{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And behold, we, etc.</b> He said <b>and behold</b> three times. Know that a dream which is a vision of prophecy and a communication from the informants who stand before HaShem — its sign and wonder is if the dream comes to the dreamer clear and bright as the shining day, so that the matter is in his eyes as though he were fully awake. The sign and the wonder come to make known that he beholds a vision of Shaddai. For dreams in which the young play are but a confusion of thought and the extravagance of the imagination. Therefore Joseph told it and said ״and behold״ in every detail, because everything he was shown was clear to his mind's eye as though he were seeing it now while awake in full possession of his faculties — and this can only be a true dream." "<b>And behold, we, etc.</b> They showed him in the dream the sheaves — these are bundles upon bundles of commandments that are performed all together. And they showed him that his bundle rises up more than all of them, by virtue of the deed that befell him with the wife of Potiphar, and also ״נִצָּבָה״ — that he was ruler and stood over all the land of Egypt. And furthermore, all the sheaves of the brothers are subdued and humbled before the merit of Joseph, for he is the thing that sustains them all, nourishing and providing for them. And he intended to make this known to them — perhaps they would remove their hatred upon knowing these things."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:24.455741659Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}